    },
    {
      "text": "Mix garlic, olive oil, salt, pepper, and thyme together in a small bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/LaI_uVNJPrTUoNEW-9WBsmZ15nA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/56352-Garlic-Prime-Rib-ddmfs-006-step3-1b0fae60c8b94edca9e2e4fe4206bdbb.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/56352/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place roast in a roasting pan with the fatty side up. Spread mixture over the top of roast; let roast sit out until it is at room temperature, no longer than 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/DH24cHrWgQ85sZyk1qLNIWoyeDQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/56352-Garlic-Prime-Rib-ddmfs-007-step4-eb655de9b644468fa8a00a923a4a7844.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/56352/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 500 degrees F (260 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake roast in the preheated oven for 30 minutes; reduce the temperature to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C), and continue roasting for an additional 60 to 75 minutes. The internal temperature of the roast should be at 135 degrees F (57 degrees C) for medium rare.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/7iCcrJkQUs1DTnhtZw3q3ypttAo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/56352-Garlic-Prime-Rib-ddmfs-007-step5-a57ca56af2a945d18d8a1e6c9e8a6aa9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/56352/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Allow roast to rest for 10 or 15 minutes before carving so the meat can retain its juices.",
